@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - Archivar</PageTitle>
<PageSeo Title="Privacy Policy - Archivar" Description="What Archivar collects, how it's used, which cookies it sets, and how to see or delete your own data." />

<div class="app-card app-legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="app-muted">Last updated: September 29, 2026.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Your account:</strong> your email, your display name and, if you set one, a securely hashed (never
            plain-text) version of your password. You can also sign in with a one-time code we email you, with no password
            at all. We record when you confirm your email and what your account's role is.</li>
        <li><strong>Feedback and contact messages:</strong> whatever you type into the Feedback button or the contact form,
            the page you sent it from, and your name and account if you were signed in.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How it's used</h2>
    <p>
        To run your account (signing you in and showing your name), to read and follow up on feedback, and - only if
        something breaks - to include relevant details in an internal error report to the site operator.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Our email provider (Azure Communication Services)</strong> - to send the one-time codes for signing in
            or confirming your email, and to notify the site operator of feedback.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>A sign-in cookie, set only if you sign in, so you don't have to sign in again on every page.</li>
        <li>A short-lived (one hour) cookie, set only while you're asking for a sign-in code, so the code only works in the
            browser that requested it.</li>
        <li>A security cookie that protects the site's forms from being submitted by other websites on your behalf.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

    <h2>Your data, your control</h2>
    <p>
        If you're signed in, visit <a href="account/data">Your data</a> to see what's stored about you and delete your
        feedback. Your email and display name are shown on <a href="account">Your account</a>, where you can confirm or
        change your email. To have your account itself deleted, use the <a href="contact">contact form</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy or your data: use our <a href="contact">contact form</a>.</p>
</div>
